# Banter in The Ghostlight Express (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is ghostlight_express): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ ghostlight_boarding_01_rook_tobin_silas
if name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and name:silas_vane and at:ghostlight_boarding and not flag.gl_crashed
interject name:rook_coldwake: That tumbled drystone wall is a textbook subsidence hazard, Tobin, and nobody's reset the fallen standing stone in a century. Poor parish upkeep, start to finish.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Never mind the masonry, Rook, look at the scarecrow planted by the yew. Sloppy stitching round the collar, and they've stuffed him with damp meadow hay that's already gone to mould.
interject name:silas_vane: Forget the straw man, we are about to board a locomotive parked on rails of actual fog. Tell me where the house keeps the brakes on a cloud.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Schedule's posted by the lychgate, Silas, so the track bed is the ferryman's jurisdiction. Just mind the turf by those iron markers as we cross.
interject name:tobin_hayward: At least they carved proper turnip lanterns for the walk up. Gives a man a warm feeling in the collarbone.
endif
-> END

~ ghostlight_g3_lounge_02_delphine_lucan_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and at:ghostlight_g3_lounge and not flag.gl_crashed
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Ebony panelling, burgundy velvet, and a Songstress at the glass who knows how to hold a room. Now this is proper headliner billing, darlings.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The upholstery is admirable, Delphine, though Dreadfang is staring rather fixedly at that jug marked with three crosses behind the bar. I suspect the vintage lacks breeding.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Never mind the spirits, Lucan, observe how the frosted sconces flatter the Druskenvalds' complexion. I would love to assay whatever preservative keeps them so charmingly poised.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He says the landscape paintings are moving when we blink, and he doesn't even have eyes. Do keep your glass vials away from the velvet, Cordelia, one spill ruins the nap.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: If you please, let us take a corner booth before the smoke thickens. It plays havoc with a hunter's nose.
endif
-> END

~ ghostlight_g4_dining_03_delphine_tobin
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:tobin_hayward and at:ghostlight_g4_dining and not flag.gl_crashed
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Six booths a side, crisp white linen, and orange bunting that looks like a third-rate harvest tent. Someone couldn't decide between a banquet and a barn dance, Tobin.
interject name:tobin_hayward: The cloth on that big eight-seat booth at the front hasn't got a crease or a crumb on it, Delphine. Whole table laid out for company that never showed.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A reserved box with no curtain call, darling, and brass-rimmed menus nobody has ever opened. Even Mrs. Calloway looks like she's waiting on a cue that missed the train.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good linen shouldn't sit idle while the dust settles on the plates. Makes my stitches itch just looking at an empty row.
endif
-> END

~ ghostlight_g5_mail_04_rook_delphine
if name:rook_coldwake and name:delphine_ravelle and at:ghostlight_g5_mail and not flag.gl_crashed
interject name:rook_coldwake: Sound filing system in here, Delphine: north pigeonholes for the dead, south for the living. Would save our parish clerk three weeks of sorting every winter.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: It is all dreadfully drab canvas, Rook, except for that bright pink envelope wedged in the north rack. Who sends boudoir stationery from the grave?
interject name:rook_coldwake: So long as the postage is squared on the docket, the colour of the paper isn't the watch's concern. Look at the Mariner hauling those sacks without a trolley.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Well, if anyone writes to me from the cheap seats beyond the veil, they had better use gilt edging. I have a reputation to keep.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Nobody's writing to me from either wall, lass. Best we leave the sorting bench clear.
endif
-> END

~ ghostlight_g6_baggage_05_rook_lucan
if name:rook_coldwake and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:ghostlight_g6_baggage and not flag.gl_crashed
interject name:rook_coldwake: Piling steamer trunks to the ceiling with barely a foot of clearance is a gross violation of gangway zoning, Lucan. One sharp bend and the whole stack comes down.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Hush now, Rook, there is a tiger of green flame asleep behind the front luggage, and it wears an iron ring upon its tail. Prime specimen, though its breathing is remarkably loud.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Open flame in an unventilated baggage car, and right beside the Druskenvalds' new leather trunks. Did nobody on this crew read the shift log?
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Dreadfang has flattened his ears at the scent, if you please, so let us step lightly past the Jailbird. I would rather not grade a flaming feline in a narrow aisle.
endif
-> END

~ ghostlight_g7_circus_06_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:ghostlight_g7_circus and not flag.gl_crashed
interject name:rook_coldwake: Rusted cages with the bars bent outward and scorched straw on the floorboards, Cordelia. Someone let the stock loose and didn't even log the damage.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Look at the thermal scoring on the iron, Rook, the specimen must have generated extraordinary internal heat before vacating. And the Harlequin overhead hasn't dropped a single beat on her trapeze.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Hanging by the knees in a moving carriage is unruly behaviour, circus or not. And don't go clicking your eyes at that marionette chest, we've no warrant to pry.
interject name:cordelia_skein: You have no poetry in your thorax, darling, though I grant you the ring of keys on that hook is a laughable security measure. Even a mindless beast could lift it.
endif
-> END

~ ghostlight_g8_tender_07_tobin_lucan
if name:tobin_hayward and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:ghostlight_g8_tender and not flag.gl_crashed
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep two paces back from that firebox, Lucan, the heat coming off the front wall is curling the straw in my cuffs. One loose spark from those pipes and I am kindling.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Step behind my coat, Tobin, if you please, the cast-iron tank is quite secure. Though I confess the soul coal drifting behind that glass porthole has a most unsettling posture.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Looks like banked embers, only cold and grey round the edges, like rot in an old stump. Nothing ought to burn without leaving clean ash for the soil.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Dreadfang will not look through the glass at all, and there is no door forward from this vestibule. Whatever feeds this furnace, friends, it was never meant to be hunted.
endif
-> END

~ ghostlight_wreckage_08_tobin_cordelia
if name:tobin_hayward and name:cordelia_skein and at:ghostlight_wreckage and flag.gl_crashed
interject name:tobin_hayward: Forty yards of good ancient oak ploughed up like a turnip furrow, and black roots pinning the engine on its side. That taproot didn't grow by accident, Cordelia, it reached up and caught us.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Fascinating pathology in the wood, Tobin, the vascular fibres have constricted around the iron boiler like a muscular spasm. And do check your cuffs, darling, your stitching survived the impact.
interject name:tobin_hayward: So it did, and not a stitch torn, while the carriages are scattered over the moss like dropped kindling. Look at that pool of soul-mist leaking into the hollow.
interject name:cordelia_skein: My vials are intact, thank goodness, though that crone-faced moon overhead is doing strange things to the ambient humours. Do hold still while I brush the oak bark from your seam.
endif
-> END
